{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"resistanceDistance","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"from","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"source","kind":"internalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"to","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"target","kind":"internalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"weight","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": (","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Edges","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Edges-swift.associatedtype","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Index","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"tolerance","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Double","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" = 1e-10, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"maxIterations","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"? = nil) ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"NoConvergence","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols13NoConvergenceV","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/NoConvergence","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Double","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"? ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"BinaryInteger","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sz","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"discussion","type":"heading","text":"Discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Conjugate gradients on the Laplacian grounded at "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"target"},{"type":"text","text":", from 0, until the residual’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Euclidean norm is at most "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tolerance"},{"type":"text","text":" (relative to the right-hand side, which has norm 1),"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"or, on a weight spread that puts that below rounding, until the true residual stops"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"improving. Jacobi preconditioned for 300 iterations, then by a modified incomplete Cholesky"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"factor in maximum-spanning-tree order. O((n + m) √κ) time; about 9 n words, and O(n + m) for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the factor when it is built."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"weight"},{"type":"text","text":" gives the conductance of the edge at each position, read once per position (every"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"position, also outside the component); a weight of 0 is no edge."}]},{"style":"note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":""},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"source"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"target"},{"type":"text","text":" are vertices of the graph, every weight is finite and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"nonnegative, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tolerance > 0"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maxIterations"},{"type":"text","text":", when given, is at least 1."}]}],"type":"aside","name":"Precondition"},{"style":"note","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"","type":"text"},{"code":"NoConvergence","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" after ","type":"text"},{"code":"maxIterations","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" conjugate-gradient iterations (one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"matrix–vector product each; 20,000 + 2n when nil), with that count and the residual’s norm","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"relative to the right-hand side’s. No input has reached the default limit in the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"measurements.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"aside","name":"Throws"}],"kind":"content"}],"kind":"symbol","variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/spectralgraphtheory\/graphprotocols\/graph\/resistancedistance(from:to:weight:tolerance:maxiterations:)-7tzs1"]}],"abstract":[{"text":"The resistance distance between ","type":"text"},{"code":"source","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"target","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (Klein and Randić 1993): the effective","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"resistance between them when each edge is a conductance (its weight; 1 without ","type":"text"},{"code":"weight:","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"),","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(e_s − e_t)ᵀ L⁺ (e_s − e_t). 0 when they are the same vertex, without reading any weight;","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"nil when they lie in different comp